# A capability declared in another module is replaced by its full name, and
# that module's own code, which names it `Ticker`, sees the replacement. BEAM
# did; the interpreter keyed the replacement `Tickers.Ticker` but looked up
# `Ticker` inside `module Tickers`, so it kept running the default.
using Tickers

main do
  IO.printLine(stamp())
  with Tickers.Ticker = FrozenTicker { at: 7 } do
    IO.printLine(stamp())
  end
  IO.printLine(stamp())
end
